            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 39-year-old male was admitted to the emergency room with a swelling of the forehead. He had a fever since 5 days and increasing pain on his forehead. He was diagnosed with Pott's puffy tumour, a complication of sinusitis.</AbstractText>
